{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/17239-scion-battle-wheel-opening-gambit","id":17239,"title":"Scion Battle Wheel - Opening Gambit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-24T12:44:24-08:00","id":17239,"title":"Scion Battle Wheel - Opening Gambit","content":"I am going to be playing Scion with a group of people who, like myself, are all new to Scion. We're trying to get the rules hammered out before we start the game, but we still have a few questions, especially about the Battle Wheel.<br /> <br /> Probably the biggest issue is that we don't quite understand how Opening Gambit interacts with the Join Battle roll and the Battle Wheel. I understand that the Scion who uses Opening Gambit goes first, and, if 2 scions use Opening Gambit, one goes &quot;firstest&quot;. But what does that look like on the Battle Wheel?<br /> <br /> For example: Suppose Scion 1 gets 10 succeses on Join Battle; Scion 2 gets 7 successes; Scion 3 gets 1 success.<br /> With just these 3, the battle wheel would start with Scion 1 on &quot;0&quot; (since he got the most successes), Scion 2 on &quot;3&quot; (since he got 3 fewer successes), and Scion 3 on &quot;6&quot; (although he got 9 fewer successes, the worst you can start on is 6).<br /> <br /> OK, assuming I got that right, let's add in Scion 4, who uses Opening Gambit. Now what would this Battle Wheel look like?<br /> <br /> Then let's add that Foe 1 also uses Opening Gambit, and beats Scion 4. What would this Battle Wheel look like?<br /> <br /> One guess we had (not necessarily our best guess, but certainly the easiest to work with) was that Scion 4 and Foe 1 count as also going on &quot;0&quot; for the purposes of determining when they get to take their next action; ie, if they are both taking speed 5 actions, they go first, then they both go next on 5. So this Battle Wheel has Foe 1 on &quot;0 the Firstest&quot;, Scion 4 on &quot;0 Firster but not Firstest&quot;, Scion 1 on just plain &quot;0&quot;, Scion 2 on &quot;3&quot;, and Scion 3 on &quot;6&quot;.<br /> <br /> Other possibilities we came up with included setting the people with Opening Gambit as effectively having 1 more success than the most successes rolled (so that, in this example, they get 11, and the Battle Wheel has Foe 1 and Scion 4 on &quot;0&quot;, Scion 1 on &quot;1&quot;, Scion 2 on &quot;4&quot;, and Scion 3 still on &quot;6&quot;), or setting all users of Opening Gambit as having 1 more Join Battle Success than the max rolled, except that the &quot;firstest&quot; one gets +2 successes (in the above example, that would put Foe 1 on &quot;0&quot;, Scion 4 on &quot;1&quot;, Scion 1 on &quot;2&quot;, Scion 2 on &quot;5&quot;, and Scion 3 on &quot;6&quot;).<br /> <br /> Does anyone know how Opening Gambit really works?<br /> <br /> As this is already a rather long post, I'll table my other questions for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1311-woody-spider-deacon","name":"Woody Spider Deacon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T12:48:08-08:00","id":17241,"title":"","content":"The guy with Opening Gambit (or guys, or gals) &quot;nudges&quot; everyone else down 1 slot. That's all. So, yes, if your highest Join Battle roll was 10, then you treat the Opening Gambit dude as if he has rolled 11.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T01:50:09-08:00","id":17607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Woody Spider Deacon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/17239-scion-battle-wheel-opening-gambit#post17239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know how Opening Gambit really works?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. It is written in a way that leaves too much open for interpretation. Telgar has already presented one interpretation that is completely valid.<br /> <br /> I honestly think the intent of the boon was for someone to 'Win' the Opening Gambit and go on Tick 0. Everyone else who did not 'Win' has to default to their ordinary Wits + Awareness result. Hence the gambling nature of it. But it is not written in a way that supports this intent.<br /> <br /> To confuse the issue further, the knack actually says nothing about moving the reaction speed of anyone else down. It is only implied by the wording of 'Go First'. Additionally, even though you get to 'Go First' the knack says nothing about when you resolve the actions that have been taken, so you could rightly conclude the knack is full of bullshit about 'Going First' and just lets you go on Tick 0 with everyone else who used it. It also does not say anything about whether anyone else can 'Go First' with you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> A razor strict reading of the rules would suggest that using Opening Gambit would allow anyone who uses it to go on Tick 0, along with whoever won the normal Wits + Awareness roll. And since there is no penalty for losing the Opening Gambit roll off besides not 'Going First', the losers either also go simultaneously or they enter a strange limbo where nobody knows when they go because they never rolled a normal join battle (but most sane storytellers will make something up).<br /> <br /> <b>I personally just say everyone who activates the knack goes on Tick 0, and forget all that nonsense about rolling against each other.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T14:01:51-08:00","id":17914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/17239-scion-battle-wheel-opening-gambit?p=17607#post17607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>I personally just say everyone who activates the knack goes on Tick 0, and forget all that nonsense about rolling against each other.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>So... if only two people are involved in the conflict, and they both activate Opening Gambit, you'd just have them both start on Tick 0, and go at the same time? Clearly not RAW, but we'll have to see how it works in play to see if it is worth the extra time and rolls to see who goes first of the first.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/17239-scion-battle-wheel-opening-gambit?p=17241#post17241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The guy with Opening Gambit (or guys, or gals) &quot;nudges&quot; everyone else down 1 slot. That's all. So, yes, if your highest Join Battle roll was 10, then you treat the Opening Gambit dude as if he has rolled 11.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you would have the Battle Wheel end up as<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">0 - Foe 1, Scion 4<br /> 1 - Scion 1<br /> 2 -<br /> 3 -<br /> 4 - Scion 2<br /> 5 -<br /> 6 - Scion 3</div> correct?<br /> <br /> As to my hopefully simpler questions about the Battle Wheel...<br /> 1) after a surprise attack / ambush, does everyone roll Join Battle, or are the ambushers considered to have already Joined Battle (on Tick 0), and everyone else rolls to... forgot the keywords... something like &quot;join battle already in progress&quot;?<br /> 2) Do I understand the rules for &quot;join battle already in progress&quot; and the math correctly that, in a battle with high (and unequal) Epic Wits, if you aren't going first, you're likely better off coming in a second late, and rolling to &quot;join battle already in progress&quot; than you are rolling to Join Battle with everyone else?<br /> <br /> To make the silliest possible example, in the above Battle Wheel (using Telgar's system), on Tick 0, Foe 1 and Scion 4 take speed 5 actions. On Tick 1, Scion 1, a Scion of monster summoning whips an egg out of his pocket and screams &quot;I choose you!&quot; Out hatches an Epic Wits 3 electric mouse kami. It takes its 4 auto-successes, rolls 4 additional Join Battle successes, and gets to go in (6-(4+4)) = 0 ticks, acting immediately. So now we have<br /> <br /> 1 - Scion 1, Summoned Mouse<br /> 2 -<br /> 3 -<br /> 4 - Scion 2<br /> 5 - Foe 1, Scion 4<br /> 6 - Scion 3<br /> <br /> To go back to my question of attacking from surprise and finish making this example crazy, if Troublemaker 1. upset that he hadn't been invited to the peace negotiations, had ambushed all parties involved, using his action and his epic strength to flick grains of rice at the goblets of the leaders of each side, knocking them over onto the peace agreement and starting this fight, would he have had to roll Join Battle, and how would adding in his ambush affect the Battle Wheel?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1311-woody-spider-deacon","name":"Woody Spider Deacon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T07:40:40-08:00","id":18403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Woody Spider Deacon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/17239-scion-battle-wheel-opening-gambit?p=17914#post17914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So... if only two people are involved in the conflict, and they both activate Opening Gambit, you'd just have them both start on Tick 0, and go at the same time? Clearly not RAW, but we'll have to see how it works in play to see if it is worth the extra time and rolls to see who goes first of the first.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, you would have the Battle Wheel end up as<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">0 - Foe 1, Scion 4<br /> 1 - Scion 1<br /> 2 -<br /> 3 -<br /> 4 - Scion 2<br /> 5 -<br /> 6 - Scion 3</div>correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how we always played it, though if two people had Opening Gambit I'd have used the rolloff to create more phantom ticks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Woody Spider Deacon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/17239-scion-battle-wheel-opening-gambit?p=17914#post17914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Do I understand the rules for &quot;join battle already in progress&quot; and the math correctly that, in a battle with high (and unequal) Epic Wits, if you aren't going first, you're likely better off coming in a second late, and rolling to &quot;join battle already in progress&quot; than you are rolling to Join Battle with everyone else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that's practically never a choice you get to make. If you know about the battle, you roll to join it as soon as it starts, even if your goal is to run far far away. If you don't know about it, how would you manage to perfectly time things so that you came in one second after it started?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Woody Spider Deacon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/17239-scion-battle-wheel-opening-gambit?p=17914#post17914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To make the silliest possible example, in the above Battle Wheel (using Telgar's system), on Tick 0, Foe 1 and Scion 4 take speed 5 actions. On Tick 1, Scion 1, a Scion of monster summoning whips an egg out of his pocket and screams &quot;I choose you!&quot; Out hatches an Epic Wits 3 electric mouse kami. It takes its 4 auto-successes, rolls 4 additional Join Battle successes, and gets to go in (6-(4+4)) = 0 ticks, acting immediately. So now we have<br /> <br /> 1 - Scion 1, Summoned Mouse<br /> 2 -<br /> 3 -<br /> 4 - Scion 2<br /> 5 - Foe 1, Scion 4<br /> 6 - Scion 3</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how we always did it when a scion used a relic to summon his familiars. Since a familiar's power level should be an order of magnitude less than a scion's it's not as powerful as it sounds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Woody Spider Deacon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/17239-scion-battle-wheel-opening-gambit?p=17914#post17914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To go back to my question of attacking from surprise and finish making this example crazy, if Troublemaker 1. upset that he hadn't been invited to the peace negotiations, had ambushed all parties involved, using his action and his epic strength to flick grains of rice at the goblets of the leaders of each side, knocking them over onto the peace agreement and starting this fight, would he have had to roll Join Battle, and how would adding in his ambush affect the Battle Wheel?</div> </div> </div> </div>I always had ambushers roll Join Battle as soon as they start the ambush. It sets their order and creates the highest JB target for the PCs to use when they get to act. I have no idea if that was RAW or not, and don't have the books handy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some online tools, including a Scion/Exalted battle wheel? <a href=\"http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/829-james-mcmurray","name":"James McMurray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T08:46:23-08:00","id":18426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James McMurray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/17239-scion-battle-wheel-opening-gambit?p=18403#post18403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but that's practically never a choice you get to make. If you know about the battle, you roll to join it as soon as it starts, even if your goal is to run far far away. If you don't know about it, how would you manage to perfectly time things so that you came in one second after it started?</div> </div> </div> </div>New one dot relic: magic blinders (rose-tinted glasses?). I never see the battle until 1 second after it starts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Not so much an intentional thing. It was more a potential issue with &quot;people who failed their perception roll to notice trouble about to start (or were further away or whatever), and then get to join battle when things go boom&quot; get to go faster than those who noticed that trouble was about to start / were there at ground zero.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James McMurray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/17239-scion-battle-wheel-opening-gambit?p=18403#post18403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always had ambushers roll Join Battle as soon as they start the ambush. It sets their order and creates the highest JB target for the PCs to use when they get to act. I have no idea if that was RAW or not, and don't have the books handy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. I've seen things like this in other systems. Although I'm pretty sure the PCs are hoping they are the ones starting the ambush most of the time, and setting the JB target for their foes!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1311-woody-spider-deacon","name":"Woody Spider Deacon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}